course: dictionary
lesson: 15190
title: One word, three meanings
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning. To find the right one, read the words around it. Those words are the context, and they leave clues.
explain: «The pizza was cut into eight sectors, and each child had one.» A sector is a slice shaped like a piece of pie. The clues are pizza and cut into eight.
explain: «The city has a busy shopping sector near the station.» Here sector means a part or area of a place. «The health sector needs more nurses.» Here sector means one part of a country's work.
explain: To check your meaning, put it into the sentence. Does «a part of the city» fit? Does «a slice of pie» fit? If it makes sense, you have found the right meaning.
fact: A sector is a part of something. It can be a slice of a circle, a part of a place, or one part of a country's work.
fact: In maths, a sector of a circle is the shape between two straight lines drawn from the centre to the edge, and the curved edge between them.
fact: Pie charts are made of sectors, and each sector shows one part of the whole.
fact: In social studies, «the public sector» means work run by the government, such as schools and hospitals. «The private sector» means work run by businesses or people.
fact: A sector of a circle has an angle at its centre point.
exercise: «The pie chart had five sectors, one for each favourite fruit.» What is a sector in this sentence? | A loud noise | A kind of fruit | *A part of a circle, like a slice of pie | A small animal
exercise: «The new park is in the north sector of the town.» What does sector mean here? | *A part or area of a place | A slice of a circle | A sum of money | A type of business
exercise: «The health sector needs more nurses.» What does sector mean here? | A type of pie | *One part of a country's work | The centre point of a circle | The edge of a town
test: «The circle was split into six equal sectors.» What is a sector here? | A type of bread | A loud sound | *A slice of the circle between two lines from its centre | A cut of meat
test: «Ben works in the private sector, for a shop owned by his family.» What does sector mean? | A type of shop | A part of a circle | A party for the family | *One part of business or work, run by people or companies
exam: Sam says the sector on his pie chart is the biggest. Which thing is a sector? | The title at the top | *The slice of the pie chart | The numbers at the bottom | The colour of the paper
